[Part 1](../soccer_1x2_gaps_1/index.html) established where the two tapes can be compared and how far apart their last trades print: Polymarket prints below Kalshi except on draws, the sign follows the taker side each print came from, and the size of the gap does not depend on the freshness cutoff. This part asks what is left once each print is given a role and charged its venue's fee: which pairing of the two tapes screens positive, in which direction, at which price, and for how much of the clock. Part 3 will ask what the prices did next.

Like part 1, this is a backward look. Each observation compares two prints that had already happened; a positive number here is a property of reference prices, not a fill.

