::: {.summary-list}

1. **Crossing both venues never pays; resting on both usually does.** Taker/taker is positive on at most {{ k.route_range.taker_taker.hi }} of observations in any group, with a mean net result of {{ k.screen.tt_pl_all_1_net }} c per contract pair in the Premier League. Maker/maker is positive on {{ k.route_range.maker_maker.lo }}–{{ k.route_range.maker_maker.hi }} with a mean net edge of {{ k.route_range.maker_maker.net_lo }} to {{ k.route_range.maker_maker.net_hi }} c. Seen after the fact, the two venues' resting-side references overlap after fees on most observations: there is spread-capture room in the reference prices. Both resting legs have to fill, and the tape does not say how often they would.

